{% comment %}
  Out-of-stock recovery.

  An out-of-stock product page was a dead end: a greyed-out OUT OF STOCK button
  and nothing else. Every visit to a sold-out line was a lost session with no way
  back, which on a pharmacy catalogue is not an edge case.

  WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT DO — read before changing the copy.

  It captures interest. It does NOT send a notification. Submissions arrive as
  contact-form emails in the Shopify admin inbox, and a person has to act on
  them. Nothing in this theme watches inventory or emails anyone when stock
  returns. That is why the wording is "tell us you want this" and never "we will
  email you when it is back" — the second is a promise the theme cannot keep.

  If the client wants real automated alerts, that needs an app (Back in Stock,
  Klaviyo) and this snippet comes out. See setup/MAINTENANCE.md.

  Uses form 'contact' because it is native, needs no app, and already carries
  Shopify's spam protection. The product is passed in hidden fields so the email
  says which line it is about.

  Accepts: product (required), variant (required)
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign form_id = 'bis-' | append: variant.id
  assign variant_label = variant.title | default: ''
  if variant_label == 'Default Title'
    assign variant_label = ''
  endif
-%}

<div class="bis" data-back-in-stock>
  {%- form 'contact', id: form_id -%}
    {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
      {%- comment -%} Shopify re-renders the page after a post, so this is the whole
          confirmation — there is no JS state to keep. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="bis-done" role="status">
        <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>
        <div>
          <strong>Thanks — we have your request.</strong>
          <span>Our team will be in touch when {{ product.title }} is back. In the meantime, a pharmacist can suggest an alternative.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      <h2 class="bis-title">Out of stock — tell us you want it</h2>
      <p class="bis-copy">
        Leave your email and our team will contact you when {{ product.title }} is
        back. This is not an automatic alert &mdash; a person from the pharmacy gets
        in touch. Nothing is ordered and you are not signed up to anything else.
      </p>

      {%- if form.errors -%}
        <div class="bis-err" role="alert">
          {{ form.errors | default_errors }}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <input type="hidden" name="contact[form_type]" value="back-in-stock">
      <input type="hidden" name="contact[product]" value="{{ product.title | escape }}{% if variant_label != blank %} — {{ variant_label | escape }}{% endif %}">
      <input type="hidden" name="contact[sku]" value="{{ variant.sku | escape }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="contact[product_url]" value="{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}?variant={{ variant.id }}">

      <div class="bis-row">
        <label class="visually-hidden" for="{{ form_id }}-email">Your email address</label>
        <input class="bis-input" id="{{ form_id }}-email" type="email" name="contact[email]"
               required autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com"
               value="{{ form.email }}">
        <button type="submit" class="bis-btn">Notify me</button>
      </div>
      <p class="bis-note">
        We use your email for this one message only. See our
        <a href="/pages/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endform -%}
</div>
